cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MIMIC: Mechanism Integration, Motion, Interlocks, and Calibration for FTC"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The Allsparks"
    alias: "FTC Team 36117"
    website: "https://github.com/The-Allsparks"
repository-code: "https://github.com/The-Allsparks/MIMIC"
url: "https://github.com/The-Allsparks/MIMIC"
abstract: >-
  MIMIC is a phased mechanism lifecycle, motion, calibration, interlock, and
  safety library for FIRST Tech Challenge robots. It begins with passive
  observation of mechanism sensors and commands and progresses through optional
  active-control phases that remain disabled until validated.
keywords:
  - FIRST Tech Challenge
  - FTC
  - mechanism control
  - motion profiling
  - homing
  - safety
  - robotics
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0-SNAPSHOT"
date-released: "2026-08-17"
